        {
          "sourceId": "columbia-southern-catalog-2026-2028-transfer-sources-2026-11-26",
          "text": "A minimum of 25% of an associate or bachelor’s degree must be completed at CSU. Transfer credit for experiential learning may not exceed 25% of the degree program."
        },
        {
          "sourceId": "columbia-southern-transfer-credit-policy-page-2026-11-26",
          "text": "Transfer credit for experiential learning may not exceed 25% of the degree program."
        },
        {
          "sourceId": "columbia-southern-sophia-agreement-2026-11-26",
          "text": "Credit will be awarded based on current transfer credit policy and the ACE recommendation at the time of completion, which is subject to change."
        }
      ],
      "basis": "CSU lists ACE-reviewed courses, credit by examination and ACE-evaluated training as sources of transfer credit separate from “Experiential or Equivalent Learning”, which its catalog defines as a Prior Learning Assessment (PLA) review. The 25% experiential-learning cap therefore limits PLA credit, not ACE-recommended courses; CSU’s published Sophia agreement awards Sophia credit under the current transfer credit policy. So ACE/NCCRS-recommended credit is limited only by the overall transfer maximum (75% of the degree).",
